"helpTitle" = "FluentScanner Help";
"helpBody" = "Enter a start and end IP and press Start (Return works too). Get IP fills the range of this machine's own subnet. A single IP scans just that host. Network (.0) and broadcast (.255) addresses are never probed.

Discovery pings every address and probes common TCP ports in parallel; live hosts then get a full port sweep. The progress bar tracks discovery; Stop halts a running scan. Export saves the table as CSV.

The dot before each IP is the device type (see the legend below the table); the brand name gets its own stable color. A shuffle icon marks a randomized MAC, which carries no vendor. The yellow row with the computer icon is this machine.

Hostnames come from Bonjour (mDNS), NetBIOS and reverse DNS. Quiet devices with no open port and no name service stay anonymous — open ports, a real MAC vendor and mDNS are what identify a device. The size-to-fit button in the toolbar (Cmd+Shift+F) fits every column to its contents.";
